I don't know if any of you know of/have played the popular "Stick
Figure RPG" Kingdom of Loathing. (http://www.kingdomofloathing.com).
It's a simple, free, rather amusing game that uses text description
and stick figure drawings for graphics; it has lots and lots of
references to various kinds of computer games and pop culture in
general.

Its latest new dungeon is called the "Enormous Greater-Than Sign." If
you follow the enormous > downward, of course you explore and get
attacked by various ASCII characters.

A sample encounter:

"At the bottom of the Enormous Greater-Than Sign, you encounter a
diminutive lowercase l.

You walk up to it, to investigate more closely, and suddenly notice
that your wallet is lighter and that the l is gone. You throw a very
stylish hissy-fit, then move on."

It's always good to see Nethack getting acknowledged round the 'Net.
Thought some of you might be amused. :)

